§ CSLv3 UNIFIED GLYPH INVENTORY
I> merged from 3 divergent v2 sources → single canonical table
I> every glyph W! have ASCII alias (J-style, §12 tokenizer compliance)
R! ← Iverson (APL): 1 glyph = 1 op • tokenizer-aligned
R! ← Egyptian determinatives: type-marker glyphs = pure semantic
R! ← Peirce Alpha: enclosure = negation
R! ← J: ASCII fallback everywhere

§ TIER-0 STRUCTURAL (flow/scope) — memorize first
| glyph | ASCII   | semantics                         |
|-------|---------|-----------------------------------|
| §     | S:      | section/module/domain boundary    |
| →     | ->      | then / yields / maps-to / flow    |
| ←     | <-      | from / sourced / derives          |
| ↔     | <->     | bidirectional / isomorphic        |
| ⇒     | =>      | implies (logical)                 |
| ⊢     | \|-     | entails / proves                  |
| ∴     | .:.     | therefore                         |
| ∵     | :..     | because                           |
| ∎     | QED     | block-end / proof-end             |

§ TIER-0 MODAL (must/may/should)
| glyph | semantics                                |
|-------|------------------------------------------|
| W!    | MUST (hard requirement, inviolable)       |
| R!    | SHOULD (strong recommend, override needs reason) |
| M?    | MAY (optional, designer discretion)       |
| N!    | MUST NOT (prohibition)                    |
| I>    | INSIGHT / key claim / important note      |
| Q?    | QUESTION / open question                  |
| P>    | PUSH FURTHER — deeper grounding requested |
| D>    | DECISION NEEDED                           |
| TODO  | unfinished, needs work                    |
| FIXME | known broken                              |

§ TIER-0 STATUS/EVIDENCE
I> merged: v2-pasted (✓◐○✗) + v2-specs (⊘△▽) + v2-root (‼)
| glyph | ASCII  | semantics                          |
|-------|--------|-------------------------------------|
| ✓     | [x]    | confirmed / true / done / verified  |
| ◐     | [~]    | partial / probable / in-progress    |
| ○     | [ ]    | pending / possible / unknown        |
| ✗     | [!]    | failed / false / blocked / rejected |
| ⊘     | [?]    | no evidence either way / TBD        |
| △     | [^]    | hypothetical / proposed             |
| ▽     | [v]    | deprecated / was-true-no-longer     |
| ‼     | [!!]   | proven / tested / immutable         |

§ TIER-0 RELATION
| glyph | semantics                              |
|-------|----------------------------------------|
| .     | tatpurusha compound (Y of X)           |
| +     | dvandva compound (X and Y)             |
| -     | karmadhāraya compound (Y that is X)    |
| ⊗     | bahuvrihi compound (having X-Y)        |
| @     | avyayibhava (at/per/in scope of)       |
| :     | bind / has / definition                |
| ::    | type-of / inherits                     |
| =     | equals / assign                        |
| !=    | not-equal                              |
| ..    | range (0..100)                         |
| ...   | continuation / variadic                |
| \|    | or / alternative / disjunction         |
| &     | explicit and (when adjacency-AND insufficient) |
| !     | emit / imperative (postfix: emit!death)|
| ?     | query / conditional / optional         |
| #     | annotation / tag / count               |
| *     | wildcard / many / collection           |
| &     | ref / pointer / alias                  |
| ^     | parent / supertype / escalate          |
| _     | slot / placeholder / anonymous         |
| /     | per / divide / reduce (APL)            |
| %     | modulo / percent                       |
| $     | variable / slot / interpolation        |
| ,     | sequence / list separator              |
| ;     | statement terminator                   |

